                "role": "assistant",
                "content": "Partial birth abortion, also known as intact dilatation and extraction (D&X), is a late-term abortion procedure that terminates a pregnancy and results in the death and intact removal of a fetus. It is typically performed when the fetus is no longer viable or due to specific medical or ethical reasons. The procedure involves dilating the cervix and extracting the fetus, which is described as \"intact\" in the documentation.  \n\nThe retrieved context highlights debates around late-term abortion, ethical considerations (e.g., sex selection, severe fetal abnormalities), and references to medical literature discussing its risks and rationale. Aftercare includes counseling to address physical and emotional recovery.  \n\nFor further reading, the documents cite sources such as *JAMA* and *Humanist* journals, which discuss the medical, ethical, and legal aspects of partial-birth abortion.",
