                "content": "The symptoms of gestational diabetes may or may not develop during pregnancy and are the same as for type 2 diabetes. They can include frequent urination, excessive thirst and hunger, weakness and fatigue, nausea and vomiting, blurred vision, hard to heal skin, gum or bladder infections, and tingling or numbness in the hands or feet.",
